// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5960 new: CVE-2026-41651 Pack2TheRoot detection rules and generic Linux LPE coverage
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5960
// Pull request author: swachchhanda000
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious SUID Bit Set on Shell Binary via Install Command
// Sigma ID: f7d2e4b9-3c18-4a67-9e05-1b6f8d3a7c52
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-04-24 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, stealth, T1548.001
// Description: Detects the use of the GNU 'install' utility to create a SUID-enabled copy of a shell binary
//   (bash, sh, dash, zsh, ksh, fish, etc.). Once a root-owned SUID shell is placed in a writable
//   location, an attacker executes it with '-p' to obtain a shell with the effective UID of root.
//   This technique works with any shell that honours the SUID bit and is used across multiple CVEs
//   and CTF/pentest scenarios. There is no legitimate operational reason to stamp a SUID bit onto a
//   shell binary via the install command.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/bash/#suid
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/install/
//   - https://github.com/Vozec/CVE-2026-41651
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/f8f8984ea4e01afa9b9a4f55559461818bd16d5a/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_install_suid_bit_set_on_shell_binary.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "/install" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-m") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "bash" or ProcessCommandLine contains " sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "dash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "zsh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ksh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "mksh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "csh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "tcsh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "fish")) and (ProcessCommandLine matches regex "-m\\s{0,5}0?[4-7]\\d{3}" or ProcessCommandLine contains "+s")
